HUNICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIMODA TATSUYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKEUCHI YASUMASA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YUDASAKA ICHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FURUSAWA, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUKI, YASUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYASHITA, SATORU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEKI, SHUNICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMODA, TATSUYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKEUCHI, YASUMASA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YUDASAKA, ICHIO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method for forming a silicon film which comprises discharging an ink composition (11) selectively onto a predetermined region of a substrate using an ink jet head (12) to form a pattern of a silicon precursor, and then subjecting the pattern to a treatment by heat and/or light to convert the silicon precursor to an amorphous silicon film or a poly-crystal silicon film. The method can be used for providing a silicon film pattern on a large area portion of a substrate with saving energy with a low cost.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé permettant de produire un film de silicium, lequel procédé consiste à libérer de façon sélective une composition d'encre (11) sur une zone prédéterminée d'un substrat à l'aide d'une tête à jet d'encre (12) de manière à créer un modèle de précurseur de silicium ; puis à soumettre ledit modèle à un traitement thermique ou à une photothérapie afin de transformer ledit précurseur de silicium en un film de silicium amorphe ou en un film de silicium poly-cristal. Le procédé selon l'invention peut être utilisé pour fournir un modèle sur une grande surface d'un substrat en économisant de l'énergie et à faible coût.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>